# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{schedule.html}, nofooter
==STA3000F: Advanced Theory of Statistics
[../../index.html Wenlong Mou], Department of Statistical Sciences, University of Toronto, Fall 2026

== Schedule
~~~
{}{table}{}
lecture | topic | references | notes ||
09\/11 | Radon--Nikodym derivatives, concentration inequalities and the probabilistic method, decision theory, admissibility and James--Stein estimation, Bayes rules | [https://www.stat.cmu.edu/~larry/=stat705/Lecture2.pdf Larry Wasserman's notes on concentration], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert%E2%80%93Varshamov_bound Gilbert--Varshamov bound] for Hamming packing, Bickel and Doksum 1.3 | [./sta3000f26-lec1.pdf Lecture 1] ||
09\/18 | Bayes and minimax decision rules, duality and admissibility, sufficient statistics, Rao--Blackwellization, factorization theorem, exponential families, introduction to UMVUE | [https://erdogdu.github.io/csc2532/latex/notes_all.pdf Murat's notes, Chapter 1], Bickel and Doksum 3.2, 3.3, Keener 3.2, [https://sites.stat.washington.edu/jaw/COURSES/580s/581/LECTNOTES/ch13.pdf Jon Wellner's notes] | [./sta3000f26-lec2.pdf Lecture 2] ||
09\/25 | complete sufficient statistics and UMVUE, Fisher information, classical and Bayesian Cramér--Rao bounds, local minimax risk | [https://sites.stat.washington.edu/jaw/COURSES/580s/581/LECTNOTES/ch13.pdf Jon Wellner's notes], Keener 3.2, 4.5, 4.6, Tsybakov 2.7.3 | [./sta3000f26-lec3.pdf Lecture 3] ||
10\/02 | local minimax and local asymptotic minimax lower bounds, Neyman--Pearson lemma and likelihood ratio tests, total variation and Pinsker's inequality, Le Cam's two-point method, monotone likelihood ratios and UMP tests | [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/b13794 Tsybakov 2.3, 2.4, 2.7.3], [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-387-93839-4 Keener 12.1--12.3], van der Vaart 8.7 | [./sta3000f26-lec4.pdf Lecture 4] ||
10\/09 | two-sided testing and UMPU tests, multivariate Gaussian testing and minimax separation, mixture-prior and chi-squared lower bounds, M-estimation and empirical risk minimization, uniform convergence, covering and packing numbers | [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-0-387-93839-4 Keener 12.5--12.7], [https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/b13794 Tsybakov 2.4, 2.7.4], van der Vaart 5.1--5.2, 19.2 | [./sta3000f26-lec5.pdf Lecture 5] ||
10\/16 | covering--packing duality and volume bounds, Wald's uniform law of large numbers and M-estimator consistency, symmetrization and Rademacher complexity, multiscale chaining and Dudley's entropy integral, uniform entropy bounds for function classes | van der Vaart 5.2, 19.2, 19.6; [https://webapps.math.uci.edu/~rvershyn/papers/HDP-book/HDP-1.pdf Vershynin (1st ed.), 4.2, 8.1] | [./sta3000f26-lec6.pdf Lecture 6] ||
10\/23 | Lipschitz-parametrized empirical processes, shattering and VC dimension, Sauer's lemma and composite classes, linear classifiers, VC covering-number bounds, VC-subgraph classes and uniform entropy | van der Vaart 19.2, 19.6; [https://webapps.math.uci.edu/~rvershyn/papers/HDP-book/HDP-1.pdf Vershynin (1st ed.), 8.2--8.3] | [./sta3000f26-lec7.pdf Lecture 7] ||
11\/06 | fat-shattering dimension and covering-number bounds, the Lipschitz function class, localized empirical processes and critical radii, convergence rates for regular and nonregular M-estimators | [https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/highdimensional-statistics/8A91ECEEC38F46DAB53E9FF8757C7A4E Wainwright 13.2, 14.3]; supplementary: [https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203275 Mendelson--Vershynin], [https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404192 Rudelson--Vershynin] | [./sta3000f26-lec8.pdf Lecture 8] ||
11\/13 | empirical-process convergence and stochastic equicontinuity, Schwartz's posterior consistency theorem, fixed-design nonparametric least squares, localized Gaussian complexity and the Lipschitz regression rate | van der Vaart 19.2; [https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/fundamentals-of-nonparametric-bayesian-inference/consistency-general-theory/97737AE50A1693E99FA472C164AC7F1E Ghosal and van der Vaart, Chapter 6]; [https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/highdimensional-statistics/8A91ECEEC38F46DAB53E9FF8757C7A4E Wainwright 13.2] | [./sta3000f26-lec9.pdf Lecture 9] ||
